From d0c8dde8996fc945fd025b7bc70722bb86171a9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Suiche <msuiche@enidon.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:24:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DeepSeek-V4.1: weightless GLP projective steering, off by
 default

h <- h - alpha*(h.d)d at the model loop's per-layer boundary (the pending
FFN write, this tree's hidden-width post-layer surface; the mHC fold is
deferred and linear in the write). Injected only when WEIGHTLESS_STEER_PATH
is configured at build time; unconfigured images are byte-identical to
stock (verified md5) - zero extra kernels, zero launches, same IR.

Loaded from a GGUF GLP sidecar with fail-closed glp.* gates (mode, hook,
width, layer map, rank, alpha multipliers). Dense zero-padded _steer_stack
by global layer id; alpha as a registered tensor buffer; glp.alpha_default
honoured unless WEIGHTLESS_STEER_ALPHA overrides. scripts/hotfix-dsv41-steering.py
is the offline validator (--check runs the same loader the engine injects).

Port of weightless's hotfix-dsv4-steering-projective.py (docs/spec/GLP.md);
serves the published GLP-39 L1-39 a0.75 vector for the 1017 checkpoint.
